---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_43",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 43,
  "text": "[[106.1]] <b>36₁.  Notae NOTAE </p>\n<p> [[106.2]] <i>A est B.</i> Copula <i>est</i>. </p>\n<p> [[106.3]] <i>Si A est B, tunc C est D. Si. Tunc.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.4]] <i>A est B. Ergo C est D. Ergo</i>, significat: </p>\n<p> [[106.5]] <i>Si A est B, tunc C est D. Atqui A est B. Ergo C est D.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.6]] <i>Atqui</i>: id est: <i>sed vera est haec propositio. ...</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.7]] <i>Sed</i>: id est: <i>praeter dictum.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.8]] Antequam pergere in Logicis contemplationibus liceat, atque inde fabricare aliquid,\n[[106.9]] prius Grammaticis opus, inprimis hic sumendus est in manus Vossii <i>Aristarchus.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.10]] Nomen substantivum et adjectivum in eo distinguuntur, quod adjectivum habet\n[[106.11]] genus ab alio rectum. Verum quia in lingua rationali careri potest generibus, ideo discrimen\n[[106.12]] etiam inter substantivum et adjectivum negligi potest. </p>\n<p> [[106.13]] Abstracta sunt substantiva ex aliis vel substantivis vel adjectivis facta; ut <i>humanitas,\n[[106.14]] pulcritudo.</i> Et <i>homo</i> est <i>habens humanitatem, pulcher habens pulchritudinem.</i> Sed in\n[[106.15]] lingua rationali videndum an non abstractis abstineri possit, aut saltem quousque possit. </p>\n<p> [[106.16]] <i>Masculus</i> est adjectivum, <i>Vir</i> est substantivum, quia pro <i>Vir</i> substitui potest <i>homo\n[[106.17]] masculus</i>; seu resolvi potest in substantivum cum Epitheto. </p>\n<p> [[106.18]] Epitheton est adjectivum substantivo cum rectione aequali junctum in eundem\n[[106.19]] terminum seu sine copula. </p>\n<p> [[106.20]] <b>Adverbia.</b> <i>Petrus scribit pulchre.</i> Id est <i>Petrus scribit aliquid pulchrum</i> seu\n [[106.21]] <i>Petrus scribit, et quod Petrus scribit est pulchrum.</i> <i>Petrus stat pulchre.</i> Id est <i>Petrus est\n[[106.22]] pulcher quatenus est stans. Petrus scribit pulchre</i>. Id est <i>Petrus est pulcher quatenus est\n[[106.23]] scribens.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.1]] <b>Pluralis.</b> <i>Homines scribunt</i>, id est <i>Titius est scribens, Cajus est scribens. Titius est\n[[107.2]] homo. Cajus est homo.</i> Vel <i>Homines scribunt</i>, id est <i>unus homo scribit, alius homo\n[[107.3]] scribit.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.4]] <b>Pronomen</b> est nomen positum in locum alterius nominis, seu designans aliud\n[[107.5]] nomen, non tamen explicando ejus attributum aliquod; sed tantum denominationem\n[[107.6]] extrinsecam ad ipsam orationem relationem. Ut <i>hic</i> id est <i>monstratus, dictus, praesens.\n[[107.7]] Ille</i> et <i>hic</i> differunt ut <i>propius</i> et <i>remotius. Ego</i> id est <i>nunc loquens. Tu</i> id est <i>nunc audiens\n[[107.8]] dictum ut audias.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.9]] Omnes illationes obliquae explicandae ex Vocum explicationibus. Ex. gr. <i>Petrus est\n[[107.10]] similis Paulo. Ergo Paulus est similis Petro.</i> Videantur talia ex Jungii <i>Logica.</i> Reducitur\n[[107.11]] ad propositiones: <i>Petrus est A nunc</i> et <i>Paulus est A nunc.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.12]] Explicandae omnes flexiones et particulae; reducendaque omnia ad simplicissimas\n[[107.13]] explicationes, quae semper salvo sensu in locum substitui possunt. </p>\n<p> [[107.14]] <b>Praepositiones</b> jungunt nomina, <b>conjunctiones</b> jungunt integras propositiones.\n [[107.16]] <i>Manus hominis</i>, id est <tab/><i>manus quae est <tab/>pars quatenus homo est <tab/>totum.</i>\n [[107.17]] <i>Manus <tab/>manus <tab/>pars <tab/>totum\n [[107.18]] filius <tab/>filius <tab/>effectus <tab/>causa\n [[107.19]] equus hominis</i> id est <tab/><i>equus <tab/>^&.v9 <Leibniz special character>qui <tab/> <tab/>^&.v- <Leibniz special character>quaeve^&.v. <Leibniz special character> est <tab/>possessio quatenus homo est <tab/>dominus\n [[107.20]] calor <tab/>calor <tab/>accidens <tab/>substantia\n [[107.21]] titulus</i> <tab/>[<i>titulus</i>] <tab/><i>praedicatum <tab/>subjectum</i>\n [[107.22]] <i>Par</i>\n [[107.23]] <i>simile</i> <i>homini</i> id est [<i>bricht ab</i>]\n [[107.24]] <i>datum</i> </p>\n",
  "number": "36₁.",
  "title": "Notae",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:36₁. Notae NOTAE A est B. Copula est. Si A est B, tunc C est D. Si. Tunc. A est B. Ergo C est D. Ergo, significat: Si A est B, tunc C est D. Atqui A est B. Ergo C est D. Atqui: id est: sed vera est haec propositio. ... Sed: id est: praeter dictum. Antequam pergere in Logicis contemplationibus liceat...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hidden data for JavaScript -->
      <script type="application/json" id="entry-data">
        {"id":"harvard_vi4_43","series":"Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)","seq":43,"text":"[[106.1]] <b>36₁.  Notae NOTAE </p>\n<p> [[106.2]] <i>A est B.</i> Copula <i>est</i>. </p>\n<p> [[106.3]] <i>Si A est B, tunc C est D. Si. Tunc.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.4]] <i>A est B. Ergo C est D. Ergo</i>, significat: </p>\n<p> [[106.5]] <i>Si A est B, tunc C est D. Atqui A est B. Ergo C est D.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.6]] <i>Atqui</i>: id est: <i>sed vera est haec propositio. ...</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.7]] <i>Sed</i>: id est: <i>praeter dictum.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.8]] Antequam pergere in Logicis contemplationibus liceat, atque inde fabricare aliquid,\n[[106.9]] prius Grammaticis opus, inprimis hic sumendus est in manus Vossii <i>Aristarchus.</i> </p>\n<p> [[106.10]] Nomen substantivum et adjectivum in eo distinguuntur, quod adjectivum habet\n[[106.11]] genus ab alio rectum. Verum quia in lingua rationali careri potest generibus, ideo discrimen\n[[106.12]] etiam inter substantivum et adjectivum negligi potest. </p>\n<p> [[106.13]] Abstracta sunt substantiva ex aliis vel substantivis vel adjectivis facta; ut <i>humanitas,\n[[106.14]] pulcritudo.</i> Et <i>homo</i> est <i>habens humanitatem, pulcher habens pulchritudinem.</i> Sed in\n[[106.15]] lingua rationali videndum an non abstractis abstineri possit, aut saltem quousque possit. </p>\n<p> [[106.16]] <i>Masculus</i> est adjectivum, <i>Vir</i> est substantivum, quia pro <i>Vir</i> substitui potest <i>homo\n[[106.17]] masculus</i>; seu resolvi potest in substantivum cum Epitheto. </p>\n<p> [[106.18]] Epitheton est adjectivum substantivo cum rectione aequali junctum in eundem\n[[106.19]] terminum seu sine copula. </p>\n<p> [[106.20]] <b>Adverbia.</b> <i>Petrus scribit pulchre.</i> Id est <i>Petrus scribit aliquid pulchrum</i> seu\n [[106.21]] <i>Petrus scribit, et quod Petrus scribit est pulchrum.</i> <i>Petrus stat pulchre.</i> Id est <i>Petrus est\n[[106.22]] pulcher quatenus est stans. Petrus scribit pulchre</i>. Id est <i>Petrus est pulcher quatenus est\n[[106.23]] scribens.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.1]] <b>Pluralis.</b> <i>Homines scribunt</i>, id est <i>Titius est scribens, Cajus est scribens. Titius est\n[[107.2]] homo. Cajus est homo.</i> Vel <i>Homines scribunt</i>, id est <i>unus homo scribit, alius homo\n[[107.3]] scribit.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.4]] <b>Pronomen</b> est nomen positum in locum alterius nominis, seu designans aliud\n[[107.5]] nomen, non tamen explicando ejus attributum aliquod; sed tantum denominationem\n[[107.6]] extrinsecam ad ipsam orationem relationem. Ut <i>hic</i> id est <i>monstratus, dictus, praesens.\n[[107.7]] Ille</i> et <i>hic</i> differunt ut <i>propius</i> et <i>remotius. Ego</i> id est <i>nunc loquens. Tu</i> id est <i>nunc audiens\n[[107.8]] dictum ut audias.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.9]] Omnes illationes obliquae explicandae ex Vocum explicationibus. Ex. gr. <i>Petrus est\n[[107.10]] similis Paulo. Ergo Paulus est similis Petro.</i> Videantur talia ex Jungii <i>Logica.</i> Reducitur\n[[107.11]] ad propositiones: <i>Petrus est A nunc</i> et <i>Paulus est A nunc.</i> </p>\n<p> [[107.12]] Explicandae omnes flexiones et particulae; reducendaque omnia ad simplicissimas\n[[107.13]] explicationes, quae semper salvo sensu in locum substitui possunt. </p>\n<p> [[107.14]] <b>Praepositiones</b> jungunt nomina, <b>conjunctiones</b> jungunt integras propositiones.\n [[107.16]] <i>Manus hominis</i>, id est <tab/><i>manus quae est <tab/>pars quatenus homo est <tab/>totum.</i>\n [[107.17]] <i>Manus <tab/>manus <tab/>pars <tab/>totum\n [[107.18]] filius <tab/>filius <tab/>effectus <tab/>causa\n [[107.19]] equus hominis</i> id est <tab/><i>equus <tab/>^&.v9 <Leibniz special character>qui <tab/> <tab/>^&.v- <Leibniz special character>quaeve^&.v. <Leibniz special character> est <tab/>possessio quatenus homo est <tab/>dominus\n [[107.20]] calor <tab/>calor <tab/>accidens <tab/>substantia\n [[107.21]] titulus</i> <tab/>[<i>titulus</i>] <tab/><i>praedicatum <tab/>subjectum</i>\n [[107.22]] <i>Par</i>\n [[107.23]] <i>simile</i> <i>homini</i> id est [<i>bricht ab</i>]\n [[107.24]] <i>datum</i> </p>\n","number":"36₁.","title":"Notae","date":null}
      </script>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers using proper regex
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[([0-9]+\.[0-9]+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Get entry data from JSON script
    const entryDataScript = document.getElementById('entry-data');
    let entryData = null;
    if (entryDataScript) {
      try {
        entryData = JSON.parse(entryDataScript.textContent);
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('Failed to parse entry data:', e);
      }
    }

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entryData && entryData.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entryData.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>